{"text": " This is my friend, Leo, and I'm trying to save her job. Are you free Tuesday evening at 9pm Amsterdam time, which I think is GMT plus 8 in your time zone? Oh, it's 3am. No! See, Leo has an almost impossible task. She has the coordinate creators from all over the world. Singapore, Australia, Canada, New York, London, Amsterdam, GMT plus 8, London. The list goes on. So, finding one time that works for everyone? Hell no. And she's not the only one. Every time my friends and I try to find a common time to meet up, let's just say it doesn't really work out. So, I knew there had to be a better way. So I decided to make something that will solve this problem for good. Meet Linkup, an app that shows where everyone is, what time it is for them, what they're working on, and based on their priorities, they can set their stages too. Any time, maybe, or maybe next time. With Linkup as a partner, Leo doesn't have to convert time zones one by one anymore. So, if you're just like Leo, or you just need a time to meet your friends, comment Linkup and I'll send you the link.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 4.34, "text": " This is my friend, Leo, and I'm trying to save her job.", "tokens": [50364, 639, 307, 452, 1277, 11, 19344, 11, 293, 286, 478, 1382, 281, 3155, 720, 1691, 13, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2869080839485958, "compression_ratio": 1.4523809523809523, "no_speech_prob": 0.024408195167779922, "words": [{"word": " This", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.36, "probability": 0.8800164461135864}, {"word": " is", "start": 0.36, "end": 0.62, "probability": 0.9953163862228394}, {"word": " my", "start": 0.62, "end": 0.8, "probability": 0.9976754784584045}, {"word": " friend,", "start": 0.8, "end": 1.14, "probability": 0.996100664138794}, {"word": " Leo,", "start": 1.24, "end": 1.42, "probability": 0.5972354412078857}, {"word": " and", "start": 1.62, "end": 2.14, "probability": 0.9605178833007812}, {"word": " I'm", "start": 2.14, "end": 2.52